From cd900bb972f06d520e4073a62f81b84ab58efd2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 09:38:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www: Reaper edits on conditionally-removed stock pages
 restored onto upstream's text

The unshipped-page list used by the replay driver and the end sweep was read from
every rm in www/Makefile, including the ones inside ifeq/ifneq blocks, so pages
this build does ship (AiMesh.asp, Advanced_FirmwareUpgrade_Content.asp,
Advanced_OperationMode_Content.asp, ...) had been reset to upstream's text and
two Reaper pages the Makefile removes only in some configurations
(Reaper_Advisor.asp, Reaper_SNMP.asp) had been dropped. Each page with a Reaper
edit is a three-way merge of the pre-rebase copy onto upstream's 40585 text; the
two Reaper pages come back verbatim. Pages with stock drift only stay upstream's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
