+/* reaper 2026-08-11: every "- -" on this page means ONE thing - that band's slot
+ * bit is clear in smart_connect_selif_x, so isSmartConnectSelifBand() is false and
+ * the row is suppressed. It does NOT mean the band has no policy: the page has
+ * already parsed wl<n>_bsd_steering_policy et al into bsd_steering_policy_array[i]
+ * for every band before it decides to print this. Rendered bare, "- -" reads as
+ * "broken" - which is exactly how it was reported from the field.
+ *
+ * Worth knowing when reading a screenshot of this page: the bit index is the
+ * band's slot in the FIXED five-slot bandName array ["2G","5G1","5G2","6G1","6G2"],
+ * not the wl unit index and not the position among the bands this router has. On a
+ * tri-band 2.4/5/6 box that means 6 GHz needs bit 3, so masks 3 and 7 render
+ * IDENTICALLY (bit 2 is 5G2, a radio that does not exist) - and shared/defaults.c
+ * ships "3" for HAS_6G models on purpose ("don't invole 6GHz band in smart connect
+ * by default"), so 6 GHz showing "- -" out of the box is stock intent, not a fault.
+ * The band selection itself lives on Wireless -> General, not here. */
