+
+/*
+	Master Smart Connect on/off toggle.
+	smart_connect_x: 0 = Disabled (each radio broadcasts independently, no band steering),
+	                 1/2/3 = Enabled (see SMRTCONN_* in shared.h). The whole Steering /
+	                 STA / Interface-Qualify / Bounce-Detect rule set on this page only takes
+	                 effect while smart_connect_x != 0, so turning it off here disables every
+	                 Smart Connect function and control at once.
+*/
+function isSmartConnectEnabled(){
+	return parseInt(variable['smart_connect_x']) > 0;
+}
+
+/* reaper v2.9.4: once cfg_server has performed the SDN migration (main network
+   on the MAINFH subunit-1 profiles), band membership is owned by the Network
+   page and the classic smart_connect_x/selif pair no longer drives anything -
+   the old toggle set nvram, fired a bare restart_wireless, and the per-band
+   profiles came back unchanged: a dead switch (owner, metal, 2026-08-30).
+   Rewriting sdn_rl from this classic page is NOT attempted - mis-serializing it
+   takes down every SSID; the SDN app owns that write. Detect the state from
+   sdn_rl itself (enum/numeric fields only, no user text). */
